      "source": [
        "## Lorenz Curve and Gini Coefficient for Math Grades (G1)\n",
        "\n",
        "The Lorenz curve is a graphical representation of the distribution of income or wealth. In this context, it will show the distribution of 'G1' (first period math grades) among students, separated by gender. The Gini coefficient is a measure of statistical dispersion intended to represent the income or wealth distribution of a nation's residents, and is the most commonly used measure of inequality. It ranges from 0 (perfect equality) to 1 (perfect inequality)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "27fe9df7",
        "outputId": "e83de209-8466-442c-9bbe-427b35a39dad"
      },
      "source": [
        "def calculate_gini(data):\n",
        "    # Sort data for Gini calculation\n",
        "    sorted_data = np.sort(data)\n",
        "    n = len(data)\n",
        "    if n == 0 or np.sum(sorted_data) == 0: # Handle empty or all-zero data\n",
        "        return 0.0\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Calculate cumulative sums\n",
        "    cum_data = np.cumsum(sorted_data)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Calculate Gini coefficient using the formula G = (1 / n) * sum((2*i - n - 1) * yi) / sum(yi)\n",
        "    # A more robust formula for calculating Gini from sorted data is:\n",
        "    # G = (2 * sum(i * yi) / (n * sum(yi))) - (n + 1) / n\n",
        "    # Where i is rank (1 to n), yi is the value.\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Using the area-based approach: G = 1 - 2 * Area_under_Lorenz_curve\n",
        "    # Area under Lorenz curve can be approximated by trapezoidal rule\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Normalized cumulative data for y-axis\n",
        "    cumulative_g1_normalized = cum_data / cum_data[-1]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Normalized cumulative population for x-axis\n",
        "    cumulative_population_normalized = np.arange(1, n + 1) / n\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Area under the Lorenz curve using trapezoidal rule\n",
        "    # Sum of (width * (height1 + height2) / 2)\n",
        "    area_lorenz = np.sum((cumulative_population_normalized - np.roll(cumulative_population_normalized, 1))[1:] * (cumulative_g1_normalized[1:] + np.roll(cumulative_g1_normalized, 1)[1:]) / 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Gini coefficient\n",
        "    gini = 1 - (2 * area_lorenz)\n",
        "    return gini\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Gini coefficient calculation function defined.\")"
      ],
